c-f4ce-4e25-8ac1-498b5963189b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2ab395a3187b48d5fcf4d77546a6621f4aaa230b9bea20a7603f477648f5b0b1","event_uuid":"09898b4a-616a-4169-b38f-31ccb8c733ad","position":{"commit_sha":"0b25a60d44353962d9093c6d374db96396cf8fe7","position":"1788912736464380001-09898b4a-616a-4169-b38f-31ccb8c733ad"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"regression","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Not starting this ticket in this session: its described implementation path and evidence target infra/terraform/user_data.sh / host gate-scratch provisioning are terraform/infra-owned, and the user explicitly prohibited touching terraform/infra because another agent owns the apply window. No claim made and no code changed.","timestamp":1788830117299992001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review PASS at 2026-09-08T20:50:39Z. Implementing with TDD in a separate worktree. Chosen source for declaration: a durable host-side config file rendered from Terraform/user_data and reconciled by a boot/systemd path after successful mount; gate admission reads that declaration source so absent markers on an attached-but-unmounted host are loud.","timestamp":1788900647808926001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation pushed as Gerrit change 2852 (PS1) at 2026-09-08T21:35:06Z. RED evidence: tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py failed on the absent-marker configured dedicated path because gate_admission had no canonical path declaration source. Fix: the canonical /var/lib/rebar/gate-scratch path configured by compose now arms the same refusal as the marker, while ordinary unmarked temp dirs still admit. Verification before push: targeted gate-scratch tests passed (15), make lint passed, and full make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=8 passed with GIT_CONFIG_* unset. Waiting for LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","timestamp":1788903308104646001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed Gerrit change 2852 (merged 2026-09-08 23:57 UTC as be40fd250fdd71319dbb2712601d0e89d6fa5c16). CI_RESULT {\"run_id\":\"34290258048\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"failure_type\":\"infra-failure\",\"failure_details\":\"Previous run 34282833154 failed closed on macOS module-size trusted-main fetch; retry on same revision passed. Earlier dispatch 34281406317 used the correct revision but hit the same trusted-main fetch/test ancestry issue.\",\"fixes_applied\":[\"no code changes; retried CI after classifying prior failure as fetch/CI infrastructure\"],\"retry_count\":1}. LLM-Review +1 at 2026-09-08 22:07 UTC; Verified +1 at 2026-09-08 23:50 UTC; unresolved comments 0. Worktree fast-forwarded to Gerrit main containing the merged commit before close.","timestamp":1788911911827365001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788610226385564881,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b0665ff0-fa33-49c6-a5b6-fdd8b1ffaf1e","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"dcc3-75ee-26ce-4840"},{"link_uuid":"efd571df-a21e-4ab0-8ea0-95cb621aa2ef","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0d51-650f-675e-4593"}],"description":"## The defect\n\n`infra/terraform/user_data.sh` protects gate scratch with a two-marker scheme, and its own comment\nstates the contract:\n\n    #   .gate-scratch-required — beside the mount point, on ROOT: the DECLARATION that\n    #     this host has a dedicated scratch volume. Survives an unmount.\n    #   .gate-scratch-mounted  — inside the mount point, on the VOLUME: the PROOF.\n    #     Disappears with the volume.\n    # Declaration present + proof absent => gate admission refuses instead of quietly\n    # repopulating the store on root.\n\n    touch \"$GATE_SCRATCH_MOUNT/../.gate-scratch-required\"\n    touch \"$GATE_SCRATCH_MOUNT/.gate-scratch-mounted\"\n\nBoth `touch`es run only AFTER a successful mount, inside `user_data.sh`, which executes **once, at\ninstance launch**. So the DECLARATION — the thing that arms the refusal — can only be written by the\nsame one-shot path that performs the mount.\n\nA volume attached to an ALREADY-RUNNING instance therefore produces neither marker. Gate admission\nthen observes \"no declaration\", concludes this host has no dedicated scratch volume, and proceeds on\nroot. Silently.\n\n## The three states, and the one that is undefended\n\n| declaration | proof | meaning | behaviour |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| present | present | mounted and healthy | proceed. Correct. |\n| present | absent | volume vanished after being provisioned | REFUSE. Correct — the case the design was built for. |\n| **absent** | absent | **host has the volume in AWS but does not know it** | **proceed on root, no complaint** |\n\nThe design distinguishes three states and defends against one. The third is not a rare edge: it is\nthe guaranteed outcome of the ordinary operational sequence \"Terraform attaches a volume to a running\ninstance\".\n\n## Confirmed live on the production host, 2026-09-05 ~11:55 UTC\n\n    $ mountpoint /var/lib/rebar/gate-scratch\n    /var/lib/rebar/gate-scratch is not a mountpoint\n\n    $ ls -la /var/lib/rebar/.gate-scratch-required\n    ls: cannot access '/var/lib/rebar/.gate-scratch-required': No such file or directory\n\n    $ ls /var/lib/rebar/gate-scratch/\n    rebar-gate-snapshots   reviewbot-vnaa57x_   semgrep-mcp   tmpgvy_yxuz   tmpqk2k1l2n.json\n\n    $ lsblk\n    nvme2n1   50G   (no fstype)      <- the gate-scratch volume: attached, raw, unmounted\n\nSo gate snapshots, a live review-bot clone and semgrep-mcp are all writing to the ROOT filesystem\nright now — the exact condition ADR 0112 provisioned this volume to end — and nothing anywhere is\nraising a word about it.\n\n## Why this is its own bug and not just `dcc3`\n\n`dcc3` is \"mount the volume\": a one-host remediation. This ticket is the reason the miss was SILENT\nrather than loud, and it recurs on every future host that acquires the volume after launch —\nincluding any replacement instance where Terraform attaches before user_data reaches its mount block,\nand any future volume added by the same pattern. Mounting the volume on this host closes `dcc3` and\nleaves this defect entirely intact.\n\nIt is also a specific instance of a pattern this repo keeps finding: a guard whose PRECONDITION is\nwritten by the very path that was skipped, so the guard cannot fire about its own absence. Compare\n`affd-913c-3fb0-40fb`, where a cross-cutting contract lived only inside a revertable commit and\nnothing detected its loss.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] The declaration is derivable from state that survives a post-launch volume attach — for example\n      the Terraform-known volume id rendered into a config the host reads, or a systemd unit that\n      reconciles markers on boot — so that \"the volume exists in AWS\" and \"the host knows it should\n      have one\" cannot diverge. State which source was chosen and why it cannot be skipped.\n- [x] The undefended state is made loud: with the volume attached and unmounted and NO declaration\n      present, gate admission refuses (or an alarm fires) rather than proceeding on root. Proven by a\n      test that constructs exactly that state.\n- [x] Defect-seeded: remove whatever new mechanism arms the declaration and confirm a test turns RED.\n      A guard never observed failing is not evidence.\n- [x] The existing two-state behaviour is unchanged — declaration+proof still proceeds, and\n      declaration-without-proof still refuses. Both pinned by tests so this change cannot silently\n      relax the case that already worked.\n- [x] Arming order is safe: the declaration must never be written on a host that cannot yet satisfy\n      it, or every gate on that box blocks. State explicitly where in the sequence it is written and\n      why that point is correct.\n- [x] Portability: host config + systemd + local tests; no CI-provider trigger.\n\n## Testing\n\n1. RED first: construct the absent/absent state and assert gate admission refuses. On current `main`\n   it proceeds, so the test fails for the right reason.\n2. Confirm present/absent still refuses and present/present still proceeds — the regression guard.\n3. Confirm the arming path cannot fire before a successful mount, so a partially-provisioned host is\n   not bricked by its own declaration.\n\n## Provenance\n\nFound while inspecting the host for `dcc3` (`dcc3-75ee-26ce-4840`), where the full measurement is\nrecorded. `dcc3` remains the \"mount this host's volume\" remediation; this ticket is why the gap was\ninvisible.\n\n## Completion evidence (2026-09-08)\n\nSource chosen: the committed compose configuration's canonical `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` path,\n`/var/lib/rebar/gate-scratch`, is now also an arming declaration in gate admission. It is\navailable to every review-bot process independently of one-shot cloud-init, so the guard no\nlonger depends on `user_data.sh` having successfully written the root-side marker after a mount.\nNoncanonical local/CI scratch paths remain unarmed unless marker files are present.\n\nRED/defect-seeded test: `test_configured_dedicated_scratch_path_refuses_without_markers` first\nfailed because gate admission had no canonical-path arming source; after the fix it proves the\nattached/unmounted/no-marker shape is loud. Removing `_CANONICAL_GATE_SCRATCH_MOUNT` makes that\ntest fail again. Existing marker behavior remains pinned by `test_gate_allows_when_required_marker_and_mount_proof_exist`\nand `test_gate_refuses_when_required_marker_exists_without_mount_proof`. `test_gate_admission_knows_the_compose_configured_dedicated_path`\npins compose/app agreement.\n\nValidation: targeted `pytest tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py -q` passed (15 tests),\n`make lint` passed, full `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=8` passed locally with `GIT_CONFIG_*` unset.\nGerrit change 2852 merged after LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0d51-650f-675e-4593"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"19b27e2c-f4ce-4e25-8ac1-498b5963189b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8ea3-3750-6772-4ac6","ticket_type":"bug","title":"The gate-scratch refusal can only arm itself at instance launch, so a volume attached to a running host lands in a silent third state the guard was never designed to see","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["812b8fda-d61b-4da9-951d-6dcab3f069fa","ef5ab151-a256-4df1-9948-498d58ceb309","fbc89f2b-7f58-4055-a62d-2af90aeb983e","7e783c6b-74d9-47dc-bf39-e33ca57a236d","3489ffa6-e93e-4706-8b26-30e84eaecbb4","db0e05b0-3d0f-4629-aed3-a6fb7be004c7","efd571df-a21e-4ab0-8ea0-95cb621aa2ef","b64bb3de-0f0b-4dd2-ba6c-caa3a4ab146a","7ce4c13c-d804-4c25-b7e2-d4a251299448","19b27e2c-f4ce-4e25-8ac1-498b5963189b","09898b4a-616a-4169-b38f-31ccb8c733ad"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788925061612943001,"uuid":"95d6f57a-c988-4244-899c-17ab39c1aad2"}